# Dependencies
node_modules/


# Build output
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# NOTE: api/ is generated from server/ by `npm run build:api`, and it is
# committed anyway — deliberately, though it looks wrong.
#
# Vercel validates the `functions` pattern in vercel.json against the cloned
# tree, before it runs the build command. An api/ that only appears during the
# build does not exist yet at that moment, and the deploy fails with "doesn't
# match any Serverless Functions".
#
# The build regenerates the directory on every deploy, so what actually ships
# is always built from the current server/ sources no matter how stale the
# committed copy is. Read and review server/; api/ is output.

# On-device inference assets (~48 MB), regenerated by `npm run setup:assets`.
# The WASM runtime is a copy of an npm dependency and the pose models are
# public downloads, so both are fully reproducible from what *is* committed.
web/public/mediapipe/
web/public/models/

# Secrets. The OpenAI key lives in the deployment environment and must never
# reach the client bundle — see the check in the README.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Materi panitia — bukan karya tim, dan repo ini publik setelah deadline.
# Tidak dibutuhkan untuk membangun atau menjalankan produk.
Datathon2026-TM_Semifinal.pdf

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local eval artifacts (regenerated by the eval scripts)
Microsoft/
AGENTS.md
eval/results/*.json
eval/results/*.png
!eval/results/.gitkeep
tts-lab/

# ...except these three. The paper cites each as the source of a
# measured number, so a judge cloning this repo has to find them.
# Two are reproducible with `npm run bench:fastloop` and
# `npm run eval:reps`; grounding.json is NOT -- it needs a live
# endpoint and an API key, so excluding it would leave the paper's
# strongest result with no evidence anyone else can reach.
!eval/results/fastloop_cost.json
!eval/results/rep_accuracy.json
!eval/results/grounding.json

# Paper sources. The deliverable is the exported PDF, not the LaTeX.
# These carry working comments (cut lists, [VERIFY] notes, page-count
# workings) that are invisible in the PDF but readable in a public repo.
docs/*.tex
